FILE: app/src/play-again.ts
```ts
import { stopAnimation, playAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function playAgain(group: AnimationGroup): void {
    stopAnimation(group);
    playAnimation(group);
}
```

I implemented `playAgain` as `stopAnimation(group)` followed by `playAnimation(group)`. Note 39 in your notes confirms this exact sequence replays a finished property group from `fromTime`, and for a non-looping glTF group (which stays at its end with `isPlaying` still true per note 27) `stopAnimation` resets `currentTime` to the start and `playAnimation` clears the stop and begins playing again. The group's `speedRatio` is untouched, so it plays at its own speed, and the pattern is repeatable. I was not unsure of anything — the notes make both cases explicit.
